  "term": "mixed-design analysis of variance",
  "definition": "A mixed-design analysis of variance is a statistical test used when a study compares both differences between groups and changes within the same participants across conditions or time. In the example here, it was used to examine the separate and combined effects of sex and mental-fatigue condition (before versus after) on landing measures.",
